            {
              "explain": "Where f(x)=0, its reciprocal is undefined and becomes unbounded.",
              "work": "\\(f(1)=0\\Rightarrow \\frac1{f(x)}\\text{ has a vertical asymptote at }x=1\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "As x approaches 0 from the right, f(x) becomes very negative, so 1/f(x) approaches 0 from below.",
              "work": "\\(\\lim_{x\\to0^+}\\frac1{f(x)}=0^-,\\quad \\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\frac1{f(x)}=0^+\\)"
            }
          ],
          "solution": "Graph A: The reciprocal has a vertical asymptote where f(x)=0 at x=1, and approaches 0 at both domain ends.",
