          "type": "mc",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "stem": "The graph of \\(y=\\cos^{-1}x\\) is transformed to a graph whose endpoints are \\((-9,\\pi)\\) and \\((-3,0)\\). Find its equation.",
          "options": [
            "\\(y=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x+6}{3}\\right)\\)",
            "\\(y=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x-2}{3}\\right)\\)",
            "\\(y=\\cos^{-1}(3x+18)\\)",
            "\\(y=\\cos^{-1}(3x-6)\\)"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "hint": "For inverse cosine, the basic endpoints are \\((1,0)\\) and \\((-1,\\pi)\\). Match these to the transformed endpoints.",
          "keyPoints": [
            {
              "text": "\\(y=\\cos^{-1}x\\)",
              "note": "The basic graph has endpoints (1, 0) and (−1, π)."
            }
